  "_notes": [
    "=============================================================================",
    "SMU DEVICE CONFIGURATION - TCP/IP CONNECTION GUIDE",
    "=============================================================================",
    "",
    "SUPPORTED DEVICE TYPES:",
    "  Keithley SourceMeter Units (SMU):",
    "    - keithley_2400, k2400       : 2400 series (single channel, ±210V, ±1.05A)",
    "    - keithley_2401, k2401       : 2401 series (single channel)",
    "    - keithley_2410, k2410       : 2410 series (single channel, ±1100V)",
    "    - keithley_2420, k2420       : 2420 series (single channel, ±60V, ±3A)",
    "    - keithley_2430, k2430       : 2430 series (single channel)",
    "    - keithley_2601b, k2601b     : 2601B series (dual channel)",
    "    - keithley_2602b, k2602b     : 2602B series (dual channel, ±40V, ±3A)",
    "    - keithley_2604b, k2604b     : 2604B series (dual channel)",
    "    - keithley_2611b, k2611b     : 2611B series (dual channel)",
    "    - keithley_2612b, k2612b     : 2612B series (dual channel, ±40V, ±10A)",
    "    - keithley_2614b, k2614b     : 2614B series (dual channel)",
    "",
    "  Keithley Picoammeter:",
    "    - keithley_6482, k6482       : 6482 picoammeter (dual channel, measure only)",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "TCP/IP VISA RESOURCE STRING FORMATS:",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  Standard TCP/IP format (most common):",
    "    TCPIP::ip_address::port::INSTR",
    "    Example: TCPIP::192.168.1.100::5025::INSTR",
    "",
    "  TCP/IP with default port (port 5025 assumed):",
    "    TCPIP::ip_address::INSTR",
    "    Example: TCPIP::192.168.1.100::INSTR",
    "",
    "  TCP/IP with hostname:",
    "    TCPIP::hostname::INSTR",
    "    Example: TCPIP::keithley-smu.local::INSTR",
    "",
    "  TCP/IP explicit board and device:",
    "    TCPIP[board]::ip_address::inst[device]::INSTR",
    "    Example: TCPIP0::192.168.1.100::inst0::INSTR",
    "",
    "  Common SCPI port numbers:",
    "    - 5025: Standard SCPI/LXI port (default for most instruments)",
    "    - 1394: Keithley 2600 series TSP (Test Script Processor) port",
    "    - Check your instrument manual for the correct port",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "OTHER VISA RESOURCE FORMATS (NON-TCP/IP):",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  USB format:",
    "    USB[board]::VendorID::ProductID::SerialNumber::INSTR",
    "    Example: USB0::0x05E6::0x2602::1234567::INSTR",
    "    - 0x05E6: Keithley Vendor ID",
    "    - Product ID varies by model (check NI MAX or device manager)",
    "",
    "  GPIB format:",
    "    GPIB[board]::primary_address::INSTR",
    "    Example: GPIB0::24::INSTR",
    "    - primary_address: Set on instrument front panel (typically 1-30)",
    "",
    "  Serial/RS-232 format:",
    "    ASRL[port]::INSTR",
    "    Example: ASRL1::INSTR (COM1)",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "CONFIGURATION FIELD DESCRIPTIONS:",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  name (string, required):",
    "    Unique identifier for the device in the system",
    "",
    "  type (string, required):",
    "    Device type identifier (see SUPPORTED DEVICE TYPES above)",
    "",
    "  visa_resource (string, required):",
    "    VISA resource string for device connection",
    "",
    "  enabled (boolean, required):",
    "    true: Device will be initialized and connected at startup",
    "    false: Device configuration is ignored",
    "",
    "  channel_count (integer, required):",
    "    Number of measurement channels",
    "    - 1 for single-channel devices (2400 series, 6482 per channel)",
    "    - 2 for dual-channel devices (2600 series, 6482 total)",
    "",
    "  enabled_channels (array of integers, required):",
    "    List of channels to enable [1] or [1, 2]",
    "",
    "  default_voltage (number, optional, SMU only):",
    "    Initial voltage setpoint in Volts",
    "",
    "  default_current (number, optional, SMU only):",
    "    Initial current setpoint in Amperes",
    "",
    "  default_compliance (number, optional, SMU only):",
    "    Initial compliance limit in Amperes (current limit for voltage source)",
    "",
    "  measurement_nplc (number, optional):",
    "    Number of Power Line Cycles for integration time",
    "    - 0.01 to 10: Common range (higher = more accurate, slower)",
    "    - 1.0: Default (one power line cycle ~16.67ms @ 60Hz)",
    "    - 10.0: High accuracy mode (~167ms per measurement)",
    "",
    "  auto_range (boolean, optional):",
    "    true: Automatic range selection (recommended)",
    "    false: Use fixed_range value",
    "",
    "  fixed_range (number, optional):",
    "    Fixed measurement range (used when auto_range = false)",
    "    Set to 0.0 when using auto_range",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "FINDING YOUR DEVICE'S IP ADDRESS:",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  Method 1: Keithley front panel",
    "    1. Press MENU on the instrument",
    "    2. Navigate to: System > Communication > LAN",
    "    3. Check IP Address, Subnet Mask, Gateway",
    "",
    "  Method 2: Use NI MAX (Measurement & Automation Explorer)",
    "    1. Install NI-VISA Runtime",
    "    2. Open NI MAX",
    "    3. Expand 'Network Devices'",
    "    4. Right-click and select 'Scan for Instruments'",
    "    5. Find your Keithley device and copy the VISA resource string",
    "",
    "  Method 3: Use find_visa_devices.exe (included in this project)",
    "    1. Build: cmake --build out/build/x64-debug --target find_visa_devices",
    "    2. Run: out\\build\\x64-debug\\find_visa_devices.exe",
    "    3. Copy the TCPIP resource string from the output",
    "",
    "  Method 4: Network scan tools",
    "    - Use tools like 'Advanced IP Scanner' or 'Angry IP Scanner'",
    "    - Look for devices with vendor name 'Keithley' or open port 5025",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "NETWORK CONNECTIVITY TROUBLESHOOTING:",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  1. Verify network connectivity:",
    "     ping 192.168.1.100",
    "",
    "  2. Check if SCPI port is accessible (Windows):",
    "     Test-NetConnection -ComputerName 192.168.1.100 -Port 5025",
    "",
    "  3. Check if SCPI port is accessible (telnet):",
    "     telnet 192.168.1.100 5025",
    "     Then type: *IDN?",
    "     Should respond with instrument identification",
    "",
    "  4. Verify firewall settings:",
    "     - Windows Defender Firewall may block outgoing connections",
    "     - Add exception for your application if needed",
    "",
    "  5. Check VISA installation:",
    "     - Verify NI-VISA Runtime is installed",
    "     - Check: where visa64.dll",
    "     - Should show: C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\visa64.dll",
    "",
    "  6. Instrument LAN settings:",
    "     - Verify instrument has valid IP address",
    "     - Check subnet mask matches your network",
    "     - Verify gateway is correct (if on different subnet)",
    "     - Try assigning static IP if DHCP fails",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "QUICK START FOR KEITHLEY 2602B VIA ETHERNET:",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  Step 1: Configure Keithley 2602B network settings",
    "    - Front panel: MENU > System > Communication > LAN",
    "    - Set IP address (e.g., 192.168.1.100)",
    "    - Note the port (usually 5025 for SCPI or 1394 for TSP)",
    "",
    "  Step 2: Test connectivity",
    "    ping 192.168.1.100",
    "",
    "  Step 3: Update this config file",
    "    {",
    "      \"name\": \"Keithley_2602B\",",
    "      \"type\": \"keithley_2602b\",",
    "      \"visa_resource\": \"TCPIP::192.168.1.100::5025::INSTR\",",
    "      \"enabled\": true,",
    "      \"channel_count\": 2,",
    "      \"enabled_channels\": [1, 2]",
    "    }",
    "",
    "  Step 4: Copy to smu_devices.json",
    "    cp config/smu_devices.example.json config/smu_devices.json",
    "    (Edit as needed for your network configuration)",
    "",
    "  Step 5: Run your application",
    "    The SMU manager will automatically connect at startup",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "DUAL-CHANNEL OPERATION (2600 SERIES):",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  Keithley 2600 series instruments have 2 independent SMU channels (A & B)",
    "",
    "  Channel mapping:",
    "    - Channel 1 = SMU Channel A",
    "    - Channel 2 = SMU Channel B",
    "",
    "  Enable both channels:",
    "    \"enabled_channels\": [1, 2]",
    "",
    "  Enable only Channel A:",
    "    \"enabled_channels\": [1]",
    "",
    "  In code:",
    "    smu->SelectChannel(1);  // Select Channel A",
    "    smu->SetVoltage(5.0);   // Set Ch A to 5V",
    "    smu->SelectChannel(2);  // Select Channel B",
    "    smu->SetVoltage(3.3);   // Set Ch B to 3.3V",
    "",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "REQUIREMENTS:",
    "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "  Software:",
    "    - NI-VISA Runtime (free download from ni.com/visa)",
    "    - Windows 10/11 (64-bit recommended)",
    "",
    "  Hardware:",
    "    - Keithley instrument with Ethernet/LAN interface",
    "    - Network connection (direct Ethernet cable or via switch/router)",
    "",
    "  Network:",
    "    - Instrument and PC on same subnet (or routing configured)",
    "    - SCPI port accessible (default: 5025)",
    "    - No firewall blocking connection",
    "",
